From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Duran <15650777+carlos-duran@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: the LAN page shows each mode's rows only on its own
 mode, and asks before leaving a session to switch

Hosts found (from Join's Look for hosts) and Disconnect showed on the
Mode row's every mode once Join or Host was on. Hosts found now shows
only while the Mode row is on Join, and Disconnect only while it is on
the mode that is on (Host or Join; Auto has none, Off leaves).

Picking another mode while others are in the session (Host with a
player, Join or Auto in a host's session, Auto hosting players) asks
first, e.g. "Disconnect from Host?" / "It switches to Join; the session
ends for the other players." Yes switches, No keeps the mode and puts
the Mode row back on it; the question closes by itself if the others
leave meanwhile. Alone, or only looking for hosts, it switches at once.
During a local wireless game only Off is allowed, as before.
---
 bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md |  2 +-
 bananads/src/menu.c       | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md b/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
index 2c4771f..488b626 100644
--- a/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
+++ b/bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@ key can also come from the environment as `BANANADS_<KEY>` (dots become undersco
 | `kms.menu` | `on` | the in-game menu (src/menu.c: SuperDrastic's, in BananaOS's colours): the menu button pauses the game and opens it on both panels. Resume, Save and Load (8 slots with pictures; a load can be undone), Quick settings (volume, brightness, the microphone's meter and a blow, Cheats, LAN multiplayer, the emulator's options), Restart game, Quit game; in a local wireless game (`wifi.local`, another handheld in it) the game keeps running behind the menu (`kms.menu_live`) and Save, Load, Restart game and Cheats are off, as are F + R / F + L. `kms.menu_test=<n>` opens it 3 s in, on the main page (1), Save (2), Load (3), Quick settings (4) or the quit question (5), for tests |
 | `kms.menu_live` | `on` | in a local wireless game the menu opens over the running game instead of pausing it (a paused handheld stops answering and the others drop it): the game gets no buttons and no touch, the top screen behind the menu keeps the frame from the moment it opened, the sound goes on; Resume, Quick settings and Quit game work, the rest is off. Once the local game has been over for 3 s the game pauses and the menu is the usual one. `off`: the menu pauses, as before |
 | `kms.menu_live_volume` | `50` | the game's sound while the menu is open over it, in % (100: unchanged) |
-| (LAN multiplayer) | | the menu's Quick settings > LAN multiplayer page (builds with `BANANADS_LAN`): Mode Off / Auto / Host / Join, Players (only with Host on the Mode row: 2-16, 4 by default, changed once Host is on, while nobody else is in its session; greyed, "Turn Host on to change it", while Host is only picked; Auto hosts with the same), Hosts found (Join: the hosts melonDS's LAN discovery hears on UDP 7063, each with its name, players and address; A joins one, the menu stays usable while it connects, up to 5 s, and says when it fails), the session's players with their ping, and Disconnect (Host and Join: a host's session ends, Off; a joined player goes back to looking for hosts). Auto has neither Players nor Disconnect: Off ends or leaves its session at once, Auto again starts afresh. With no Wi-Fi network, Quick settings' row says "No Wi-Fi" in grey and doesn't open; an open page turns its rows off and says to connect in BananaOS's Settings > Network. Auto says what it is doing: waiting for the game, looking for a host of this game, hosting, in a host's session (a desktop melonDS host said as such), the game online (WFC), or stopped by a problem (and when it tries again). The mode changes without a restart while no local wireless game is on; during one only Disconnect works (Auto: Off), after a question. The choice is kept in `wifi.local` and `wifi.local_players`; `BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL` or `BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL_PLAYERS` in the environment (BananaLinux: `/data/banana/bananads.env`) still win at each start, and the page says so while one is set |
+| (LAN multiplayer) | | the menu's Quick settings > LAN multiplayer page (builds with `BANANADS_LAN`): Mode Off / Auto / Host / Join, Players (only with Host on the Mode row: 2-16, 4 by default, changed once Host is on, while nobody else is in its session; greyed, "Turn Host on to change it", while Host is only picked; Auto hosts with the same), Hosts found (Join: the hosts melonDS's LAN discovery hears on UDP 7063, each with its name, players and address; A joins one, the menu stays usable while it connects, up to 5 s, and says when it fails), the session's players with their ping, and Disconnect (Host and Join: a host's session ends, Off; a joined player goes back to looking for hosts). Hosts found shows only with Join on the Mode row (Join on), Disconnect only on the Mode row of the mode that is on. Another mode picked while others are in the session (Host with a player, Join or Auto in a host's session, Auto hosting players) asks first ("Disconnect from Host and switch to Join?", No keeps the mode); alone, or only looking, it switches at once. Auto has neither Players nor Disconnect: Off ends or leaves its session at once, Auto again starts afresh. With no Wi-Fi network, Quick settings' row says "No Wi-Fi" in grey and doesn't open; an open page turns its rows off and says to connect in BananaOS's Settings > Network. Auto says what it is doing: waiting for the game, looking for a host of this game, hosting, in a host's session (a desktop melonDS host said as such), the game online (WFC), or stopped by a problem (and when it tries again). The mode changes without a restart while no local wireless game is on; during one only Disconnect works (Auto: Off), after a question. The choice is kept in `wifi.local` and `wifi.local_players`; `BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL` or `BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL_PLAYERS` in the environment (BananaLinux: `/data/banana/bananads.env`) still win at each start, and the page says so while one is set |
 | `kms.queue` | `2` | the most finished frames waiting for the screen (1-3); past that the oldest is dropped. Frames are committed one per refresh, so a game whose frames take 19 and 12 ms in turn still shows a new one at every refresh |
 | `kms.rt` | `on` | the presenter (the thread that commits the frames) at `SCHED_FIFO` 5, below the sound thread, as SuperDrastic's: a late wake-up finds the last flip still pending and the frame waits a refresh |
 | `kms.stats` | `0` | every this many frames shown, log the rate of new frames on the panels, the frames emulated per second, the refreshes that showed no new frame and the frames dropped |
diff --git a/bananads/src/menu.c b/bananads/src/menu.c
index c59b638..5261e12 100644
--- a/bananads/src/menu.c
+++ b/bananads/src/menu.c
@@ -476,7 +476,7 @@ static void play(int id) { if (snd_ok[id] && H.sound_play) H.sound_play(H.ctx, i
 
 /* ---------- state ---------- */
 enum { SC_MAIN, SC_SAVE, SC_LOAD, SC_SET, SC_QUIT, SC_OVERWRITE, SC_BUSY, SC_MIC, SC_RESTART, SC_CHEAT,
-       SC_LAN, SC_LAN_HOSTS, SC_LAN_LEAVE };
+       SC_LAN, SC_LAN_HOSTS, SC_LAN_LEAVE, SC_LAN_SWITCH };
 static int enabled = -1, inited, open_, scr, sel_main, sel_slot, sel_set, dirty_top, dirty_bot;
 static char busy_msg[96];
 
@@ -759,7 +759,8 @@ static int cheats_off(void) { return mp_locked; }   /* a code changes the game t
  * outside a local wireless game; in one, Disconnect is all there is (in Auto, Off; the others' game shows its own
  * error). The pages: SC_LAN (Mode, Players (Host), Hosts found (Join), Disconnect (Host and Join), and the state),
  * SC_LAN_HOSTS (the hosts on the network, a scrolling list as Cheats'), SC_LAN_LEAVE (are you sure, in a local
- * wireless game). Auto has no Players (a session it hosts has Host's size, wifi.local_players) and no Disconnect:
+ * wireless game), SC_LAN_SWITCH (another mode while others are in the session: are you sure). Each mode's rows show
+ * only with that mode on the Mode row: Hosts found (Join), Disconnect (the mode that is on). Auto has no Players (a session it hosts has Host's size, wifi.local_players) and no Disconnect:
  * Off leaves (the others hear it at once), Auto again starts afresh */
 static bmenu_lan LS;
 static int lan_pick, lan_max_pick, sel_lan, sel_host, top_host, lan_joining;
@@ -771,6 +772,8 @@ enum { LR_MODE, LR_PLAYERS, LR_HOSTS, LR_LEAVE };
 static int lrows[4], nlrows;
 static int lan_locked(void) { return live_ || (H.mp_lock && H.mp_lock(H.ctx)); }   /* a local wireless game is on */
 /* Auto in a local wireless game: the Mode row offers Off (asked first, as a Disconnect), nothing else */
+/* others in the session (a host's guests, or a host we joined): another mode asks first (SC_LAN_SWITCH) */
+static int lan_with_others(void) { return LS.state == BM_LAN_READY && (LS.nplayers > 1 || !lan_hosting()); }
 static int lan_auto_off_only(void) { return LS.mode == BM_LAN_AUTO && !LS.no_net && lan_locked(); }
 static int lan_poll(void) {   /* the frontend's state into LS; 1: it changed */
     static bmenu_lan n;
@@ -786,8 +789,8 @@ static int lan_poll(void) {   /* the frontend's state into LS; 1: it changed */
 static void lan_rows(void) {
     nlrows = 0; lrows[nlrows++] = LR_MODE;
     if (lan_pick == BM_LAN_HOST) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_PLAYERS;   /* (the Mode row on Host; greyed till Host is on) */
-    if (LS.mode == BM_LAN_JOIN && LS.state != BM_LAN_READY) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_HOSTS;
-    if ((LS.mode == BM_LAN_HOST || LS.mode == BM_LAN_JOIN) && LS.state == BM_LAN_READY) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_LEAVE;
+    if (lan_pick == BM_LAN_JOIN && LS.mode == BM_LAN_JOIN && LS.state != BM_LAN_READY) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_HOSTS;
+    if (lan_pick == LS.mode && (LS.mode == BM_LAN_HOST || LS.mode == BM_LAN_JOIN) && LS.state == BM_LAN_READY) lrows[nlrows++] = LR_LEAVE;
     if (sel_lan >= nlrows) sel_lan = nlrows - 1;
 }
 static void lan_open(void) {   /* Quick settings > LAN multiplayer */
@@ -854,7 +857,7 @@ static void draw_bottom(void) {
     canvas *c = &CV[1];
     dots(c, 0, 0, c->w, c->h, C_BG, C_DOT);
     int gx0 = S(20), gx1 = c->w - S(20), gy0 = S(58), gy1 = S(404), bw = S(3) < 2 ? 2 : S(3);
-    int s = scr == SC_OVERWRITE ? SC_SAVE : (scr == SC_QUIT || scr == SC_RESTART) ? SC_MAIN : scr == SC_LAN_LEAVE ? SC_LAN : scr;
+    int s = scr == SC_OVERWRITE ? SC_SAVE : (scr == SC_QUIT || scr == SC_RESTART) ? SC_MAIN : (scr == SC_LAN_LEAVE || scr == SC_LAN_SWITCH) ? SC_LAN : scr;
     if (scr == SC_BUSY) {
         draw_header(c, "Please wait", "", 0);
         int w = S(420), h = S(150), x0 = (c->w - w) / 2, y0 = S(150);
@@ -1232,6 +1235,15 @@ static void draw_bottom(void) {
     else if (scr == SC_RESTART)
         dialog(c, "Restart the game?", "Back to the title screen. Anything since your last save will be lost.",
                "Keep playing", "Restart", 1);
+    else if (scr == SC_LAN_SWITCH) {
+        char t[96], b[160];
+        const int h = lan_hosting();
+        snprintf(t, sizeof t, "Disconnect from %s?", lang_tr(lan_mode_name[LS.mode]));
+        if (lan_pick == BM_LAN_OFF) snprintf(b, sizeof b, "%s", h ? "It turns off; the session ends for the other players." : "It turns off; you leave the host's session.");
+        else snprintf(b, sizeof b, h ? "It switches to %s; the session ends for the other players." : "It switches to %s; you leave the host's session.",
+                      lang_tr(lan_mode_name[lan_pick]));
+        dialog(c, t, b, "No", "Yes", 1);
+    }
     else if (scr == SC_LAN_LEAVE)
         dialog(c, lan_hosting() ? "End the session?" : "Leave the session?",
                "A local wireless game is on: it stops for the other players too (their game shows its own error).",
@@ -1306,7 +1318,11 @@ static void lan_activate(void) {
     }
     if (locked) { play(SND_BACK); mlog("[menu] LAN: no mode change in a local wireless game\n"); return; }
     if (LS.no_net) { play(SND_BACK); mlog("[menu] LAN: no Wi-Fi\n"); return; }
+    if (id == LR_MODE && lan_pick != LS.mode && lan_with_others() && scr != SC_LAN_SWITCH) {   /* asked first */
+        scr = SC_LAN_SWITCH; play(SND_SELECT); dirty_bot = 1; return;
+    }
     if (id == LR_MODE && lan_pick != LS.mode) {
+        scr = SC_LAN;
         mlog("[menu] LAN: %s\n", lan_pick == BM_LAN_HOST ? "host" : lan_pick == BM_LAN_JOIN ? "look for hosts"
                                  : lan_pick == BM_LAN_AUTO ? "auto" : "off");
         H.lan_set(H.ctx, lan_pick, lan_pick == BM_LAN_HOST ? lan_max_pick : 0, "");   /* (Auto: Host's size) */
@@ -1389,6 +1405,7 @@ static void activate(void) {
     case SC_LAN: lan_activate(); break;
     case SC_LAN_HOSTS: lan_join(sel_host); break;
     case SC_LAN_LEAVE: lan_leave(); break;
+    case SC_LAN_SWITCH: lan_activate(); break;   /* Yes: the mode picked */
     case SC_MIC:
         /* the game has to run to hear it: back to the game, with a pop-up for as long as it blows */
         play(SND_SELECT); if (H.blow) H.blow(H.ctx, 3000); close_menu();
@@ -1411,6 +1428,7 @@ static void back(void) {
     case SC_QUIT: case SC_RESTART: scr = SC_MAIN; dirty_bot = 1; break;
     case SC_MIC: case SC_CHEAT: case SC_LAN: scr = SC_SET; dirty_bot = 1; break;
     case SC_LAN_HOSTS: case SC_LAN_LEAVE: scr = SC_LAN; dirty_bot = 1; break;
+    case SC_LAN_SWITCH: lan_pick = LS.mode; scr = SC_LAN; dirty_bot = 1; break;   /* No: the mode stays */
     default: scr = SC_MAIN; dirty_top = dirty_bot = 1; break;
     }
 }
@@ -1456,7 +1474,7 @@ static void nav(int dx, int dy) {
     if (moved) { play(SND_MOVE); dirty_bot = 1; }
 }
 static void tap(int px, int py) {               /* a touch-down on the bottom panel, in panel pixels */
-    if (scr == SC_OVERWRITE || scr == SC_QUIT || scr == SC_RESTART || scr == SC_LAN_LEAVE) {
+    if (scr == SC_OVERWRITE || scr == SC_QUIT || scr == SC_RESTART || scr == SC_LAN_LEAVE || scr == SC_LAN_SWITCH) {
         if (in_rect(R_DLG_A, px, py)) activate(); else if (in_rect(R_DLG_B, px, py)) back();
         return;
     }
@@ -1549,10 +1567,11 @@ int bmenu_run(int start) {
         while (open_ && H.poll(H.ctx, &e)) handle(&e);
         if (open_ && held_dir && now_ms() >= rep_next) { nav(rep_dx, rep_dy); rep_next = now_ms() + 110; }
         { static long long mt; if (scr == SC_MIC && now_ms() - mt >= 33) { mt = now_ms(); dirty_bot = 1; } }   /* the meter moves */
-        if ((scr == SC_LAN || scr == SC_LAN_HOSTS || scr == SC_LAN_LEAVE || scr == SC_SET) && now_ms() - lan_polled >= 500) {
+        if ((scr == SC_LAN || scr == SC_LAN_HOSTS || scr == SC_LAN_LEAVE || scr == SC_LAN_SWITCH || scr == SC_SET) && now_ms() - lan_polled >= 500) {
             if (lan_poll()) dirty_bot = 1;   /* the LAN's state, twice a second; a join done: back to the page */
             if (scr == SC_LAN_HOSTS && lan_joining && !(LS.state == BM_LAN_BUSY && LS.addr[0])) { lan_joining = 0; scr = SC_LAN; sel_lan = 0; dirty_bot = 1; }
             if (scr == SC_LAN_LEAVE && LS.state != BM_LAN_READY) { scr = SC_LAN; dirty_bot = 1; }
+            if (scr == SC_LAN_SWITCH && (!lan_with_others() || lan_locked())) { scr = SC_LAN; dirty_bot = 1; }   /* nobody left: no question */
             if (scr == SC_LAN_HOSTS && LS.no_net) { lan_joining = 0; scr = SC_LAN; sel_lan = 0; dirty_bot = 1; }   /* the network went */
         }
         { static long long vt; if (scr == SC_SET && now_ms() - vt >= 500) { vt = now_ms(); want_ex(-1, -1, 1); }   /* the volume keys' */
